# TailwindCSS + DaisyUI Frontend Rules

- Use Tailwind utility classes as the default styling approach.
- Prefer DaisyUI components for common UI patterns before writing custom markup.
- Avoid ad hoc custom CSS unless utilities or DaisyUI cannot express the requirement.
- Keep className strings readable; group layout, spacing, color, and state variants consistently.
- Use responsive variants (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) instead of separate breakpoint-specific components.
- Centralize theme tokens in Tailwind/DaisyUI config rather than hardcoding repeated values.

## Example
```tsx
<button className="btn btn-primary w-full md:w-auto">Save</button>
```
